Hi,

I would like to know if it's ok to use .Internal(inspect(x)) in order
to detect vector copying.

Take for example the following silly code:

f <- function() {
  x = seq(10)
  print(.Internal(inspect(x)))
  for(i in seq(10)) {
    x[i] <- x[i] + 1
    print(.Internal(inspect(x)))
  }
}

The output of f() was:

